**Integrating Error Reporting**

I've examined the code to ensure seamless error message integration when folder name changes fail. The `saveFolderEdit` function now includes robust error checking to provide clear feedback. This change significantly enhances user experience. I'm prioritizing displaying informative feedback when saving an empty folder name or encountering deletion issues. Next, I'll test these scenarios.


**Improving Error Feedback Loop**

I'm working to enhance the error handling within the folder editing process. I'm focusing on making the error messaging more informative and user-friendly, to improve the feedback loop. My goal is to ensure that users understand why a specific action, such as a save or delete, failed. The focus is to integrate error messages smoothly into the UI and make the overall experience more intuitive. I'm prioritizing seamless integration of visual cues within the application.


**Enabling Manual Folder Creation**

I've realized that the "Yeni Klasör" button is hidden when the folder list is empty, preventing a user from manually creating an empty folder. My focus is now on ensuring this button is always visible. I'm exploring adding a "Yeni Klasör" button to the welcome screen, providing users the option to create a new folder anytime, regardless of the folder list's state. I need to make sure the app offers an intuitive way to add a folder.


**Enabling Empty Folder Creation**

I've revised the `renderDashboard` function to ensure that the "Yeni Klasör" button is always visible. The current design restricts creating the first folder until another folder already exists. Now, I'm making the button available at all times. This will allow the user to manually create the first empty folder. This will be the next step, ensuring that this update aligns with the visual design.


**Enhancing Error Messages**

I'm now integrating error messaging into the "create folder" flow. The error handling will alert the user when the folder name is empty upon saving. My immediate focus is providing an informative message, and ensuring the interface responds appropriately to these user actions. I'm focusing on ensuring users understand when there are issues creating folders with invalid names.

